.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rqx-update 1  "update " 
.SH NAME
rqx\-update \- Install the newest release, or say what it would change
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrqx update\fR [\fB\-\-check\fR] [\fB\-\-notes\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-motion\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR] [\fB\-\-progress\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Install the newest release, or say what it would change
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
Report whether a newer release exists and stop
.TP
\fB\-\-notes\fR
Print the release notes for the newest release
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR \fI<X.Y.Z>\fR
Install this release, such as 1.2.3, instead of the newest
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the method, the URLs and the file that would be replaced, and change nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR
Never open the interactive interface; bare `rqx` prints the report instead
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR
Leave the mouse to the terminal. The session never captures it; the flag is still accepted so an existing invocation keeps working
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour output; `auto` follows NO_COLOR and whether stdout is a terminal
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-motion\fR \fI<MOTION>\fR [default: on]
Animation in the interactive interface
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR
Do not draw the progress bar on stderr; `\-\-quiet` implies it
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI<PROGRESS>\fR [default: auto]
How a scan reports progress on stderr; `plain` prints a line every two seconds for a job log
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: A bar on a terminal, nothing in CI or when stderr is redirected
.IP \(bu 2
bar: A bar whenever stderr is a terminal, CI included
.IP \(bu 2
plain: A line on stderr every two seconds and at each phase, for a job log
.IP \(bu 2
none: Nothing
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  rqx update                          install the newest release
  rqx update \-\-check                  say whether one exists, install nothing
  rqx update \-\-notes                  read what changed
  rqx update \-\-version 1.2.3          install that release, newer or older
  rqx update \-\-dry\-run                show how and from where, change nothing
